    * This case is in the "valid" array; since tests pass, the parser no longer concatenates JSDoc tags into the requirement ID and no spurious error is reported.,Implementation of JSDoc boundary detection (REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION / REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE):
  - File: src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts
  - New helper:
    /**
     * Detect whether a normalized comment line starts with a non-traceability JSDoc tag.
     * ...
     * @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
     * @req REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION
     * @req REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE
     */
    export function isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): boolean {
      const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
      if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
        return false;
      }
      if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
        return false;
      }
      return true;
    }
  - This matches the story’s solution approach: recognizing any JSDoc tag pattern (@word) as a boundary, except the traceability tags themselves.,Annotation line normalization (supports continuation logic and termination):
  - File: src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts
  - normalizeCommentLine:
    export function normalizeCommentLine(rawLine: string): string {
      const trimmed = rawLine.trim();
      if (!trimmed) return "";
      const annotationMatch = trimmed.match(/@story\b|@req\b|@supports\b/);
      if (!annotationMatch || annotationMatch.index === undefined) {
        const withoutLeadingStar = trimmed.replace(/^\*\s?/, "");
        return withoutLeadingStar;
      }
      return trimmed.slice(annotationMatch.index);
    }
  - Combined with isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine and the passing multi-line tests, this implements:
    * REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION (stop at JSDoc-tag boundaries),
    * REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC (only continue when the next line does not start with a JSDoc tag),
    * REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE (multi-line values preserved until a boundary).,Documentation updated to describe JSDoc coexistence (AC: Documentation):
  - File: docs/rules/valid-annotation-format.md
  - Section "JSDoc coexistence":
    - States that traceability annotations can appear before, after, or interleaved with other JSDoc tags.
    - States: "The parser treats any JSDoc tag line that starts with `@` (other than `@story`, `@req`, or `@supports`) as a boundary that terminates the current multi-line traceability value. Continuation lines are only considered part of the same annotation if they do not start with another JSDoc tag. This prevents JSDoc tags from being concatenated into requirement IDs ... eliminating false positives like `REQ-OPTIMIZATION@param{object}data`."
    - Provides a concrete code example with @story/@req followed by @param/@returns, matching the story’s requested examples.,Global regression / backward compatibility signal:
